  66:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *
  67:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  HAS_DEDICATED_PRINT_PORT      if defined and equal to 1, indicate that a dedicated COM port is 
  68:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *                                for the log services.
  69:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  USE_PRINTF_FROM_TOOL          if defined, indicate that the LC_PRINT(..) function is mapped on 
  70:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *                                printf(..) implementation from the SDK/tool-chain else low-cost i
  71:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *                                used (lc_print())
  72:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *
  73:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  USE_RETARGET_IO_FROM_TOOL     if defined (and ==1) indicates that the retarget-io feature is na
  74:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *                                supported by the SDK/tool-chain (not provided by the aiValidation
  75:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *
  76:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  Notes:
  77:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *    - aiTestUtility.c implements the Low-level character I/O (output only) function for the print
  78:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *      It is mapped on the serial port (port_io_write() fct). This serial port is also used to exc
  79:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *      the binary messages (nanopb format, aiValidation app) with the HOST. When the AI COM stack 
  80:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *      characters are no more forwarded on this serial port, they are skipped (_ioWriteAllowed=fal
  81:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *      support is always requested, a dedicated serial port can be defined (port_io_dedicated_writ
  82:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *    - setting of the serial ports should be done by the main application code.
  83:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *
  84:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  port_io_dedicated_putc(b)     write a byte to the dedicated COM port (blocking mode)
  85:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  port_io_dedicated_write(&b,n) write n byte(s) to the dedicated COM port (blocking mode)
  86:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *
  87:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  port_io_get(&d, timeout)      wait byte from the default COM port
  88:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  port_io_write(&b, n)          write n byte(s) to the default COM port (blocking mode)
  89:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  *  port_io_read(&b, n)           read n byte(s) from the default COM port (blocking) mode
  90:SR5E1_AI_Demo_7000P/lib/misc/inc/ai_device_adaptor.h ****  */
